  "body": "#3406 adds part-in-spindle mode to a `Kind::Mill` setup. The mill spindle holds the stock, and lathe tools stand on the table at their own work offsets. Turning operations generate and simulate in that setup.\n\nToday the program gate refuses the post of such a setup by name (`part_in_spindle::program_problems` in `crates/app/src/part_in_spindle.rs`). No post section writes what the setup needs. A turning section through a milling post comes out as milling.\n\nAdd the post section:\n\n- Write the stock's length offset with `G43 H<h_register>` from `SetupDef::part_in_spindle`.\n- Select each table tool's own work offset from its station (`TableStation::work_offset`).\n- Turn the spindle with the station's direction (`M3` or `M4`).\n- Write the X words for the station's approach side (`-X` or `+X`) in radius, as a mill control reads them.\n- Refuse by name a turning operation whose tool has no table station.\n- Remove the program-gate refusal for a setup that the post section can write.\n\nDone means: a part-in-spindle program posts through a milling post with these words, a golden pins the output, and a tool without a station is refused by name.\n\nPart of #2580\n",
